# 🏏 Cricket Performance Analytics

## 📌 Project Overview
This project focuses on analyzing cricket performance data across multiple formats — ODI, Test, and T20 cricket — using Python-based data analytics techniques. The analysis aims to uncover player consistency, batting dominance, bowling efficiency, and cross-format performance trends through data cleaning, exploratory data analysis (EDA), visualization, and statistical insights.

The project was developed using Google Colab and includes cleaned datasets, visual analytics, and performance-based metrics to derive meaningful cricket insights.

---

# 🎯 Problem Statement
Modern cricket performance varies significantly across ODI, Test, and T20 formats. Teams, selectors, analysts, and fans require data-driven insights to evaluate player consistency, batting aggression, bowling effectiveness, and tournament dominance across formats.

This project aims to analyze historical cricket statistics to identify:
- Top-performing batsmen and bowlers
- Cross-format player performance trends
- Batting and bowling efficiency
- Strategic insights from cricket statistics

---

# 📂 Dataset Information
The dataset contains historical cricket statistics across multiple formats:

### ODI Datasets
- ODI Batting Statistics
- ODI Bowling Statistics
- ODI Tournament Data

### Test Datasets
- Test Batting Statistics
- Test Bowling Statistics
- Test Tournament Data

### T20 Datasets
- T20 Batting Statistics
- T20 Bowling Statistics
- T20 Tournament Data

